  planner_response {
    thinking: "**Defining Front-End Architecture**\n\nI\'m now diving into the front-end architecture, focusing on a modular TypeScript approach within the `/src` directory. Specifically, I\'m defining a `/src/types.ts` file. It will contain essential data structures such as `LandDimensions`, which will include width, height, unit (meters or feet), and shape (rectangular, L-shaped, oval, or polygon).\n\n\n**Refining Data Structures**\n\nI\'m expanding the `/src/types.ts` file. I\'ve defined `EstablishmentCategory`, `EstablishmentVariable` (a catalog entry for establishments with default properties like dimensions and category), and `PlacedEstablishment` (an instance on the land with specific coordinates and instance-specific properties). I\'m carefully considering how to represent dimensions, rotation, and revenue in these definitions.\n\n\n**Defining Road & Waypoint Data**\n\nI\'m currently working on detailed definitions for roads and waypoints. I\'ve defined `RoadPoint`, `RoadPath`, and `Waypoint` with their respective properties. I am representing roads with `points`, `width`, `roadType` and `color`. Waypoints will have `type`, coordinates, `icon`, `color`, and optional `targetConnections`. I\'m also considering `isLocked` and a `customLabel` for more customizable features.\n\n\n**Defining UI Settings**\n\nI\'ve been thinking about UI settings, specifically regarding visibility. I\'m working to define `legendVisible`, `labelsVisible`, `blueprintMode`, and `dimensionsVisible` as boolean variables. I\'m aiming for clean and simple user controls.\n\n**Incorporating Preset Data & Exports**\n\nNow I\'m focusing on `/src/data/defaultVariables.ts`, populating it with a rich catalog of establishment variables, including dimensions. I\'m also adding sample preset land templates for quick starts. Finally, I am defining SVG and PNG export functions in `/src/utils/exportUtils.ts`. High resolution exports will also be supported.\n\n\n**Expanding Utility Functions**\n\nI\'m now focusing on utility functions. I\'m adding functions for JSON project save and load in `/src/utils/`. Furthermore, I\'m working on spatial utility functions for collision detection, distance calculations, alignments, and spatial metrics in `/src/utils/spatialUtils.ts`. My attention is also focused on the image export utilities, making sure exports and downloads are clear and crisp. I\'m also planning to incorporate a title block and legend.\n\n\n**Designing Interactive Canvas**\n\nI\'m now focusing on `/src/components/CanvasMap.tsx`, creating the interactive SVG canvas visualizer with pan, zoom, and grid lines. It will render land boundaries, roads, waypoints, and establishments with rotation and size handles. I am building select/edit, draw road, place waypoint, and zone overlay modes, with real-time collision highlighting for overlaps and fire corridor warnings. A context toolbar is being designed for item editing, including dimension adjustments, rotation, and alignment tools.\n\n\n"
    thinking_duration {
      seconds: 11
      nanos: 160550436
    }
    stop_reason: STOP_REASON_STOP_PATTERN
  }
}
